    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Swahili-style reckoning adopted (standard in Kenyan vernaculars; 9:00 = 'thaa ithatũ'), hours rotated by 6. Additive '<hour> na ndagĩka <minutes in words>' form, 'na nuthu' for half; no past/to system used. Numerals: ithano, ikũmi, mĩrongo ĩĩrĩ/ĩtatũ/ĩna/ĩtano. Minute numerals in class-10 concord with ndagĩka are my best reading; quarter rendered as 'ndagĩka ikũmi na ithano'."
